eb.git) and is empty here; cloning it fails outside GitHub and the web UI will not load locally.","Java version mismatch: CI builds on Java 21 while release and Docker images use JDK 25.","Schema changes need Liquibase changelogs that work on H2, MySQL, PostgreSQL and SQL Server; unit tests run against H2/memory only, so cross-database breakage is not caught.","tools/test-integration.py and other Python tools need a running server and are not run by CI; they can rot without notice.","docker/compose/*.yaml contain demo database password 'traccar'; a secret scanner may flag them (they are examples, not real secrets).","Many commits go straight to master; a harness that assumes PR review may not match current practice.","The protocol package is very large (about 680 files); agents may duplicate helpers instead of reusing BaseProtocolDecoder, Parser, BitUtil and similar helpers."],"notes_for_apply":"Runtime: JDK 21 (temurin, as in .github/workflows/gradle.yml); the Gradle wrapper downloads Gradle 9.8.2. Install and build with ./gradlew assemble (outputs target/tracker-server.jar and target/lib/). Fast gate: ./gradlew test. Full gate: ./gradlew check (CI runs ./gradlew build = assemble + check, including Checkstyle). One test: ./gradlew test --tests org.traccar.protocol.Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest. Run locally: java -jar target/tracker-server.jar debug.xml (H2 database in target/, web on port 8082, web UI needs the traccar-web submodule, which is empty here). Network access to Maven Central is required at configuration time. Keep Gradle as the task runner; for 'dev', add a JavaExec task named run in build.gradle instead of a Makefile, and do not change existing tasks, versions, the jar manifest or the dependencyUpdates/enforcer rules. Do not touch schema/changelog-*.xml (released migrations), setup/ or release.yml except to document them. Test status was not run in this assessment; if a test fails, mark it @Disabled with a reason and record it in docs/harness/log.md. Docs must follow the existing style: Apache license header on new Java files, 4-space indentation (.editorconfig). Commit messages: short imperative subject, no prefix. Use uw-harness TODO blocks for deploy and observability unknowns."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":936,"cache_read_input_tokens":58333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":936},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4ebb02b-ffa0-4c59-b7ef-afe895946a2f","uuid":"97582cb3-f8d9-4a60-a22e-82ebcd4b33f8","timestamp":"2026-11-01T16:24:36.284Z","request_id":"req_011CgcWtfur9qDwezEMegeS6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RB5A6FmvsCuPA6uz7pyeP6":{"project":{"name":"Traccar (tracker-server)","one_liner":"Open source GPS tracking server in Java that decodes 200+ device protocols, stores positions in an SQL database and exposes a REST/WebSocket API for the Traccar web and mobile apps.","value_proposition":"Traccar lets anyone track vehicles, assets or people with almost any GPS tracker on the market, without vendor lock-in. One self-hosted (or managed) server receives data from 2000+ device models, keeps the history in a standard SQL database, and gives users live maps, reports, geofences, alarms and notifications through a REST API and the web dashboard.","users":["Fleet operators and dispatchers who follow vehicles in real time and read reports","GPS tracking resellers who run a white-label Traccar platform for their customers","Individuals who track their own devices","Administrators who self-host and configure the server (traccar.xml, database, protocols)","Integrators who consume the REST API, WebSocket stream, MCP endpoint or event forwarders (Kafka, MQTT, AMQP, Redis, HTTP)"],"use_cases":[{"name":"Receive and decode device data","description":"Trackers connect over TCP/UDP/HTTP/MQTT on per-protocol ports; a Netty pipeline frames and decodes the binary or text messages into Position objects.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/ServerManager.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/TrackerServer.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/BasePipelineFactory.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/*ProtocolDecoder.java (e.g. Gt06ProtocolDecoder.java)"]},{"name":"Process and store positions","description":"Decoded positions go through a handler chain (filter, time, distance, motion, engine hours, geocoding, geofences, speed limits, computed attributes) and are written to the database, sometimes in batches.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/ProcessingHandler.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/handler/","src/main/java/org/traccar/database/PositionBatchWriter.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/storage/DatabaseStorage.java"]},{"name":"Generate events and send notifications","description":"Event handlers detect alarms, geofence enter/exit, overspeed, ignition, maintenance and more; notificators send them by email, SMS, Firebase push, Telegram, Pushover, WhatsApp or web.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/handler/events/","src/main/java/org/traccar/notification/","src/main/java/org/traccar/notificators/","templates/notifications/"]},{"name":"Manage accounts, devices and permissions via REST API","description":"Jersey resources under /api manage users, devices, groups, drivers, geofences, calendars, attributes, maintenance, notifications, permissions, sessions and shares; documented in openapi.yaml.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/","src/main/java/org/traccar/api/security/","openapi.yaml","src/main/java/org/traccar/web/WebServer.java"]},{"name":"Live tracking in the web dashboard","description":"Jetty serves the traccar-web frontend and a WebSocket that pushes live positions, events and device status.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/api/AsyncSocket.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/api/AsyncSocketServlet.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/session/ConnectionManager.java","traccar-web (git submodule, empty in this checkout)"]},{"name":"Reports and exports","description":"Route, events, trips, stops, summary, geofence and combined reports, with Excel (jxls templates), CSV, GPX and KML export, and scheduled reports by email.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/ReportResource.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/reports/","templates/export/","src/main/java/org/traccar/schedule/TaskReports.java"]},{"name":"Send commands to devices","description":"Users send commands (engine stop, reboot, custom) that protocol encoders translate to device-specific messages, queued when the device is offline.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/CommandResource.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/database/CommandsManager.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/*ProtocolEncoder.java"]},{"name":"Forward data to other systems","description":"Positions and events are forwarded to Kafka, MQTT, AMQP, Redis, Wialon or HTTP URLs.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/forward/","src/main/java/org/traccar/handler/PositionForwardingHandler.java"]},{"name":"Authentication and single sign-on","description":"Login with password, TOTP, LDAP or OpenID Connect; OAuth clients; MCP endpoint for AI tools.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/SessionResource.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/OidcResource.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/database/LdapProvider.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/database/OpenIdProvider.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/web/McpServerHolder.java"]},{"name":"Background jobs and health","description":"Scheduled tasks for device inactivity, expirations, session timeout, cleanup of temporary data, health check and WebSocket keepalive; /api/health endpoint.","entry_points":["src/main/java/org/traccar/schedule/ScheduleManager.java","src/main/java/org/traccar/api/resource/HealthResource.java"]}],"glossary":[{"term":"Position","meaning":"One decoded location fix from a device (time, coordinates, speed, course, plus free-form attributes). Model in org.traccar.model.Position."},{"term":"Device","meaning":"A tracker identified by its uniqueId (usually IMEI)."},{"term":"Protocol decoder / encoder","meaning":"Per-protocol Netty handler that turns raw device bytes into Positions (decoder) or commands into device bytes (encoder). Around 680 files in org.traccar.protocol."},{"term":"Frame decoder","meaning":"Netty handler that splits the byte stream into complete device messages before the protocol decoder."},{"term":"Handler","meaning":"Processing step applied to every Position after decoding (org.traccar.handler), e.g. FilterHandler, GeofenceHandler."},{"term":"Event","meaning":"Something derived from positions (alarm, geofence enter/exit, overspeed, ignition on/off, device online/offline)."},{"term":"Notificator","meaning":"Delivery channel for event notifications (mail, SMS, Firebase, Telegram, Pushover, WhatsApp, web, command)."},{"term":"Forwarder","meaning":"Component that sends positions or events to an external system (Kafka, MQTT, AMQP, Redis, URL, Wialon)."},{"term":"Computed attribute","meaning":"User-defined JEXL expression evaluated on each position to create derived attributes."},{"term":"Geofence","meaning":"Geographic area (circle, polygon, polyline) that triggers enter/exit events."},{"term":"Server (model)","meaning":"The single global settings record of the instance, not a host."},{"term":"Keys","meaning":"org.traccar.config.Keys: the documented catalogue of every configuration key in traccar.xml."},{"term":"debug.xml / traccar.xml","meaning":"Java properties XML configuration files; debug.xml is the local development config used by default by Main, setup/traccar.xml is the packaged default."},{"term":"Broadcast service","meaning":"Cluster synchronisation of cache updates between several Traccar nodes via Redis or multicast."},{"term":"Plus codes","meaning":"Open Location Code offline geocoder used in debug.xml (geocoder.type=pluscodes)."},{"term":"MCP","meaning":"Model Context Protocol endpoint exposing the API to AI tools (web.mcp.enable)."}]},"stack":{"languages":["Java 21 (build target; release builds use JDK 25)","Python 3 (tools/ scripts for integration and performance testing)","Shell"],"frameworks":["Gradle 9.8.2 (wrapper)","Netty 4.2 (device networking)","Jetty 12.1 + Jersey 4 (HTTP, REST, WebSocket)","Guice 7 (dependency injection)","Jackson","Liquibase 5 (schema migrations, schema/changelog-*.xml)","HikariCP","jxls / Apache POI and Velocity (reports and notification templates)","JUnit Jupiter 6 + Mockito 5","Checkstyle 14.4 (gradle/checkstyle.xml)","Protocol Buffers"],"datastores":["H2 (default, embedded file database)","MySQL / MariaDB","PostgreSQL / TimescaleDB (docker/compose/traccar-timescaledb.yaml)","Microsoft SQL Server","Redis (optional broadcast and forwarding)"],"external_services":["Geocoding providers (Google, Nominatim, Here, Mapbox, OpenCage, etc. in org.traccar.geocoder)","Geolocation providers (org.traccar.geolocation)","AWS SNS (SMS)","Firebase Cloud Messaging","Telegram, Pushover, WhatsApp","SMTP mail","Kafka, MQTT (HiveMQ), RabbitMQ AMQP","LDAP and OpenID Connect providers","Azure Identity (SQL Server auth)","Docker Hub and ghcr.io (release images)","DigitalOcean Spaces S3 (preview builds) and GitHub Releases"]},"architecture":{"components":[{"name":"Tracker server (protocol layer)","kind":"service","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/ (ServerManager.java, TrackerServer.java, BasePipelineFactory.java, protocol/)","tech":"Java 21, Netty","description":"Opens one TCP/UDP/HTTP/MQTT listener per enabled protocol, frames and decodes device messages into Positions, encodes commands back to devices."},{"name":"Processing pipeline","kind":"library","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/handler/, ProcessingHandler.java","tech":"Java, Guice","description":"Chain of position handlers and event handlers (filter, geocoder, geofence, motion, speed limit, computed attributes, alarms)."},{"name":"Web server and REST API","kind":"api","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/web/, src/main/java/org/traccar/api/","tech":"Jetty 12, Jersey 4, Jackson","description":"Serves /api REST resources (openapi.yaml), WebSocket live updates, the MCP endpoint, the static web app and an optional H2 console."},{"name":"Web frontend","kind":"frontend","path":"traccar-web (git submodule, not checked out)","tech":"Separate repository traccar/traccar-web, built with npm in release.yml","description":"Browser dashboard served by the web server from web.path."},{"name":"Storage layer","kind":"library","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/storage/, schema/","tech":"JDBC, HikariCP, Liquibase","description":"DatabaseStorage builds SQL queries for model objects; Liquibase changelogs in schema/ migrate the tc_* tables at startup. MemoryStorage for in-memory mode."},{"name":"SQL database","kind":"database","path":"configured in debug.xml / traccar.xml","tech":"H2 by default; MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, SQL Server","description":"Stores users, devices, positions, events, geofences, settings."},{"name":"Scheduler","kind":"scheduler","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/schedule/","tech":"Java executor","description":"Periodic tasks: inactivity checks, expirations, scheduled reports, cleanup, health check, keepalive."},{"name":"Notifications","kind":"service","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/notification/, notificators/, templates/notifications/","tech":"Velocity, Jakarta Mail, AWS SNS, Firebase","description":"Formats and sends event notifications through several channels."},{"name":"Forwarders","kind":"integration","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/forward/","tech":"Kafka, MQTT, AMQP, Redis, HTTP","description":"Push positions and events to external systems."},{"name":"Reports","kind":"library","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/reports/, templates/export/","tech":"jxls, POI","description":"Report providers and file exports (xlsx, CSV, GPX, KML)."},{"name":"Broadcast service","kind":"integration","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/broadcast/","tech":"Redis or UDP multicast","description":"Keeps caches consistent between clustered instances."},{"name":"Geocoder / geolocation","kind":"integration","path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/geocoder/, geolocation/","tech":"HTTP clients","description":"Reverse geocoding and cell/wifi geolocation through external providers."},{"name":"Packaging and release","kind":"ci","path":".github/workflows/release.yml, setup/, docker/","tech":"GitHub Actions, makeself, Inno Setup, jlink, Docker","description":"Builds Linux/Windows installers and Alpine/Debian/Ubuntu Docker images, smoke tests them, publishes to S3, GitHub Releases, Docker Hub and ghcr.io."},{"name":"Dev tools","kind":"tooling","path":"tools/","tech":"Python 3, shell","description":"Integration test that sends sample messages to a running server, performance, command and trip test scripts, config doc generator."}],"mermaid":"flowchart LR\n  devices[\"GPS trackers\"] -->|TCP/UDP/HTTP/MQTT| proto[\"Netty protocol decoders\"]\n  proto --> pipe[\"Handler pipeline\"]\n  pipe --> storage[\"Storage layer + Liquibase\"]\n  storage --> db[(\"SQL DB: H2/MySQL/Postgres/MSSQL\")]\n  pipe --> events[\"Event handlers\"]\n  events --> notif[\"Notificators\"]\n  notif --> ext_notif[\"Mail/SMS/Firebase/Telegram\"]\n  pipe --> fwd[\"Forwarders\"]\n  fwd --> ext_fwd[\"Kafka/MQTT/AMQP/Redis/HTTP\"]\n  pipe --> geo[\"Geocoders\"]\n  geo --> ext_geo[\"Geocoding APIs\"]\n  web[\"Jetty web server + REST/WebSocket/MCP\"] --> storage\n  web --> reports[\"Reports\"]\n  reports --> storage\n  frontend[\"traccar-web frontend\"] -->|REST + WebSocket| web\n  sched[\"Scheduler\"] --> storage\n  sched --> notif\n  web -->|commands| proto\n  bcast[\"Broadcast service\"] <-->|Redis/multicast| other[\"Other Traccar nodes\"]\n  web --> bcast\n  relea