ks` in AGENTS.md and docs/local-dev.md (Gradle has no setup target to install it automatically)."},{"id":"local-env","status":"fail","evidence":["docker/compose/traccar-mysql.yaml and traccar-timescaledb.yaml exist but run the published traccar/traccar image, not the local build","debug.xml: H2 file database in ./target/database, so no external store is required","Main.java defaults to ./debug.xml when no argument is given","No Gradle run/dev task"],"gap":"The checker found no root compose file and no dev/run target; local run is a manual java -jar command.","plan":"Add a Gradle JavaExec task named `run` (mainClass org.traccar.Main, args debug.xml, dependsOn classes) in build.gradle without changing existing tasks; add a root compose.yaml with an optional MySQL or PostgreSQL service for testing other databases; write docs/local-dev.md (JDK 21, ./gradlew assemble, run with debug.xml, web UI on :8082 needs the traccar-web submodule, reset by deleting target/database*, logs on console, H2 console at /console)."},{"id":"env-example","status":"fail","evidence":["config/Config.java:48 reads CONFIG_USE_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES; compose files use DATABASE_DRIVER, DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_USER, DATABASE_PASSWORD","No .env file tracked; compose files contain demo password 'traccar'"],"gap":"No .env.example documenting environment-variable configuration.","plan":"Create .env.example with CONFIG_USE_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES=true, DATABASE_DRIVER=org.h2.Driver, DATABASE_URL=jdbc:h2:./target/database, DATABASE_USER=sa, DATABASE_PASSWORD= and a comment that any key in config/Keys.java maps to an upper-case env variable. Main configuration stays in debug.xml/traccar.xml."},{"id":"toolchain-pinned","status":"fail","evidence":["build.gradle: sourceCompatibility/targetCompatibility JavaVersion.VERSION_21, enforcer maxJdkVersion 21","gradle.yml uses Java 21; release.yml and Dockerfiles use JDK 25"],"gap":"Java version is set in build.gradle but no version file the checker recognises.","plan":"Add .java-version containing 21 (or a .sdkmanrc with java=21-tem) to match CI. Optionally add a Gradle java toolchain block; ask the team whether 21 or 25 is preferred."},{"id":"deploy-explicit","status":"partial","evidence":[".github/workflows/release.yml: manual workflow_dispatch builds installers, smoke tests them, publishes to DigitalOcean Spaces (preview) or GitHub Releases, pushes Docker images to Docker Hub and ghcr.io","docker/Dockerfile.{alpine,debian,ubuntu}, setup/ (setup.sh, traccar.service, traccar.iss, cloud-init.yaml)"],"gap":"Release artifacts and pipeline exist but are not documented; how the managed hosting is deployed is not visible.","plan":"Write docs/deploy.md: environments (self-host installers, Docker images, managed hosting = TODO), how a release is built (bump Implementation-Version in build.gradle, schema changelog, run Build Release with a version input), what is published where, smoke test in the workflow, rollback (TODO), who can deploy (TODO). Use uw-harness TODO blocks for unknowns."},{"id":"observability","status":"fail","evidence":["Logging: slf4j-jdk14, logger.* keys in config/Keys.java (console, file, level, rotate, fullStackTraces)","HealthResource.java: GET /api/health checks message rate and database","compose healthcheck uses /api/health; schedule/TaskHealthCheck.java","StatisticsResource / StatisticsManager"],"gap":"No observability doc; where production logs and alerts live is not visible.","plan":"Write docs/observability.md: logging config and default logs/ folder, /api/health semantics (web.healthCheck.dropThreshold), statistics API, TaskHealthCheck, web request log; TODO blocks for log storage, dashboards and alert channel of the managed service."},{"id":"skills","status":"fail","evidence":["No .agents/skills/ or .claude/skills/"],"gap":"No skills.","plan":"Create .agents/skills/implement-change, add-protocol-decoder (decoder + frame decoder + registration + *ProtocolDecoderTest with hex samples, run single test), debug-local (run with debug.xml, logger.fullStackTraces, H2 console, tools/test-integration.py / hex.sh to send sample messages), add-schema-change (new Liquibase changelog), and release (pointing to docs/deploy.md and its TODOs). Symlink .claude/skills to .agents/skills."}],"questions":[{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"How is the managed hosting (traccar.org pricing) and the demo server deployed and updated: from the Docker images, installers, or another pipeline outside this repository?","why":"release.yml only publishes artifacts; production rollout is not visible."},{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Who is allowed to run the 'Build Release' workflow, and how is a bad release rolled back (re-tag, previous Docker tag, schema rollback)?","why":"Needed for the deploy doc and the release skill; Liquibase migrations make rollback non-trivial."},{"requirement":"observability","question":"For the managed service, where are logs, metrics and alerts kept, and which signal tells you production is broken (only /api/health, or something else)?","why":"The code shows logging and a health endpoint but no external monitoring."},{"requirement":"agreements","question":"Should outside contributors and agents always open a pull request, while maintainers keep committing directly to master as the history shows?","why":"Defines the branch rule written into CONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md."},{"requirement":"agreements","question":"What is the definition of done for a protocol change: is a decoder test with a real device sample always required, and must tools/test-integration.py also pass?","why":"Most changes are protocol decoders; the rule decides what agents must verify."},{"requirement":"toolchain-pinned","question":"Which Java version should developers use: 21 (CI and build.gradle) or 25 (release builds and Docker images)?","why":"The version file must match the intended toolchain."},{"requirement":"local-env","question":"Should local development check out the traccar-web submodule (relative URL ../traccar-web.git), or is the backend usually run without the web UI?","why":"debug.xml points web.path to ./traccar-web/simple, which is empty in this checkout."}],"risks":["build.gradle resolves Jersey transitive versions at configuration time (resolveTransitiveVersion), so every Gradle invocation, even listing tasks, needs network access to Maven Central.","./gradlew test runs about 426 test classes; it may take minutes, which is slow for a 'fast' gate and a pre-push hook.","Checkstyle is part of ./gradlew check and build: any style violation fails CI, so agents must follow gradle/checkstyle.xml.","The traccar-web submodule uses a relative URL (../traccar-web.git) and is empty here; cloning it fails outside GitHub and the web UI will not load locally.","Java version mismatch: CI builds on Java 21 while release and Docker images use JDK 25.","Schema changes need Liquibase changelogs that work on H2, MySQL, PostgreSQL and SQL Server; unit tests run against H2/memory only, so cross-database breakage is not caught.","tools/test-integration.py and other Python tools need a running server and are not run by CI; they can rot without notice.","docker/compose/*.yaml contain demo database password 'traccar'; a secret scanner may flag them (they are examples, not real secrets).","Many commits go straight to master; a harness that assumes PR review may not match current practice.","The protocol package is very large (about 680 files); agents may duplicate helpers instead of reusing BaseProtocolDecoder, Parser, BitUtil and similar helpers."],"notes_for_apply":"Runtime: JDK 21 (temurin, as in .github/workflows/gradle.yml); the Gradle wrapper downloads Gradle 9.8.2. Install and build with ./gradlew assemble (outputs target/tracker-server.jar and target/lib/). Fast gate: ./gradlew test. Full gate: ./gradlew check (CI runs ./gradlew build = assemble + check, including Checkstyle). One test: ./gradlew test --tests org.traccar.protocol.Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest. Run locally: java -jar target/tracker-server.jar debug.xml (H2 database in target/, web on port 8082, web UI needs the traccar-web submodule, which is empty here). Network access to Maven Central is required at configuration time. Keep Gradle as the task runner; for 'dev', add a JavaExec task named run in build.gradle instead of a Makefile, and do not change existing tasks, versions, the jar manifest or the dependencyUpdates/enforcer rules. Do not touch schema/changelog-*.xml (released migrations), setup/ or release.yml except to document them. Test status was not run in this assessment; if a test fails, mark it @Disabled with a reason and record it in docs/harness/log.md. Docs must follow the existing style: Apache license header on new Java files, 4-space indentation (.editorconfig). Commit messages: short imperative subject, no prefix. Use uw-harness TODO blocks for deploy and observability unknowns."}}}
