derTest with hex samples, run single test), debug-local (run with debug.xml, logger.fullStackTraces, H2 console, tools/test-integration.py / hex.sh to send sample messages), add-schema-change (new Liquibase changelog), and release (pointing to docs/deploy.md and its TODOs). Symlink .claude/skills to .agents/skills."}],"questions":[{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"How is the managed hosting (traccar.org pricing) and the demo server deployed and updated: from the Docker images, installers, or another pipeline outside this repository?","why":"release.yml only publishes artifacts; production rollout is not visible."},{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Who is allowed to run the 'Build Release' workflow, and how is a bad release rolled back (re-tag, previous Docker tag, schema rollback)?","why":"Needed for the deploy doc and the release skill; Liquibase migrations make rollback non-trivial."},{"requirement":"observability","question":"For the managed service, where are logs, metrics and alerts kept, and which signal tells you production is broken (only /api/health, or something else)?","why":"The code shows logging and a health endpoint but no external monitoring."},{"requirement":"agreements","question":"Should outside contributors and agents always open a pull request, while maintainers keep committing directly to master as the history shows?","why":"Defines the branch rule written into CONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md."},{"requirement":"agreements","question":"What is the definition of done for a protocol change: is a decoder test with a real device sample always required, and must tools/test-integration.py also pass?","why":"Most changes are protocol decoders; the rule decides what agents must verify."},{"requirement":"toolchain-pinned","question":"Which Java version should developers use: 21 (CI and build.gradle) or 25 (release builds and Docker images)?","why":"The version file must match the intended toolchain."},{"requirement":"local-env","question":"Should local development check out the traccar-web submodule (relative URL ../traccar-web.git), or is the backend usually run without the web UI?","why":"debug.xml points web.path to ./traccar-web/simple, which is empty in this checkout."}],"risks":["build.gradle resolves Jersey transitive versions at configuration time (resolveTransitiveVersion), so every Gradle invocation, even listing tasks, needs network access to Maven Central.","./gradlew test runs about 426 test classes; it may take minutes, which is slow for a 'fast' gate and a pre-push hook.","Checkstyle is part of ./gradlew check and build: any style violation fails CI, so agents must follow gradle/checkstyle.xml.","The traccar-web submodule uses a relative URL (../traccar-web.git) and is empty here; cloning it fails outside GitHub and the web UI will not load locally.","Java version mismatch: CI builds on Java 21 while release and Docker images use JDK 25.","Schema changes need Liquibase changelogs that work on H2, MySQL, PostgreSQL and SQL Server; unit tests run against H2/memory only, so cross-database breakage is not caught.","tools/test-integration.py and other Python tools need a running server and are not run by CI; they can rot without notice.","docker/compose/*.yaml contain demo database password 'traccar'; a secret scanner may flag them (they are examples, not real secrets).","Many commits go straight to master; a harness that assumes PR review may not match current practice.","The protocol package is very large (about 680 files); agents may duplicate helpers instead of reusing BaseProtocolDecoder, Parser, BitUtil and similar helpers."],"notes_for_apply":"Runtime: JDK 21 (temurin, as in .github/workflows/gradle.yml); the Gradle wrapper downloads Gradle 9.8.2. Install and build with ./gradlew assemble (outputs target/tracker-server.jar and target/lib/). Fast gate: ./gradlew test. Full gate: ./gradlew check (CI runs ./gradlew build = assemble + check, including Checkstyle). One test: ./gradlew test --tests org.traccar.protocol.Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest. Run locally: java -jar target/tracker-server.jar debug.xml (H2 database in target/, web on port 8082, web UI needs the traccar-web submodule, which is empty here). Network access to Maven Central is required at configuration time. Keep Gradle as the task runner; for 'dev', add a JavaExec task named run in build.gradle instead of a Makefile, and do not change existing tasks, versions, the jar manifest or the dependencyUpdates/enforcer rules. Do not touch schema/changelog-*.xml (released migrations), setup/ or release.yml except to document them. Test status was not run in this assessment; if a test fails, mark it @Disabled with a reason and record it in docs/harness/log.md. Docs must follow the existing style: Apache license header on new Java files, 4-space indentation (.editorconfig). Commit messages: short imperative subject, no prefix. Use uw-harness TODO blocks for deploy and observability unknowns."},"ttft_ms":2398,"type":"result","duration_ms":150762,"uuid":"7877c356-4c5e-4c22-a6e2-79f902d3c624","ttft_stream_ms":2307,"time_to_request_ms":220,"first_content_frame_ms":2307,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":16490,"cacheReadInputTokens":347074,"cacheCreationInputTokens":59269,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8734308,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2547,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":59269,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
